raction and task prediction under the fixed data and compute protocol.\",\n  \"architecture_search\": {\n    \"scope\": \"Whole-model design, including replacement of the initial network and all internal representations.\",\n    \"design_dimensions\": [\n      \"Representation units: fields, events, behavior groups, learned slots and target/task tokens.\",\n      \"Information flow: stacked interaction, layer-wise joint interaction, parallel exchange, learned routing or other testable unified structures.\",\n      \"History selection/compression jointly designed with target/context-conditioned retrieval.\",\n      \"Derived features computed from authorized inputs: field matches, behavior counts/composition, grouping and sequence positions.\",\n      \"Shared and task-conditioned representations, prediction readouts and registered training-loss mechanisms.\"\n    ],\n    \"lineage\": \"parent_trial identifies a comparison and evidence lineage; it does not require code or architectural inheritance. inherited_components may be empty when the whole model is replaced.\",\n    \"proposal_unit\": \"A coherent mechanism hypothesis can require several coordinated structural changes. Build that structure and plan component, replacement or factorial controls to identify where its value comes from.\",\n    \"evidence\": \"Select by the equal-weight validation AUC mean across click, cart, favorite and purchase; report macro Logloss and every task change. Use that same rule for checkpoints, parents, topic gains, merge eligibility and final selection. Evaluate mechanism support, nearest-work differences and measured cost; compare closest architectural alternatives and the initial reference.\",\n    \"fixed_contracts\": \"Available sample information, labels, data split, scoring, resource accounting and the frozen host training recipe remain shared. Internal architecture and readout design are candidate choices.\",\n    \"reference_use\": \"UniRank comparison methods provide inspe