d and unknown state does not permit duplicate execution. If costs exceed estimates, reduce optional attribution/assessment repetitions explicitly, report the limitation, and stop when no useful admissible experiment fits. This phase performs syntax/source checks only; no local training, installations or withheld assessment.'\n}}\n\nnotes=(\\\"Host reproduction: import the standalone module, instantiate Model(feature_map, **CONFIG), and execute the frozen trainer bound to protocol \\\"+protocol+\\\"; the host training CLI is not exposed. Local syntax command: python3 -m py_compile candidate.py control_shared_wide.py. Numerical gates are pending: four finite [B,1] predictions and finite sum-BCE backward in FP32/BF16; batch8192 peak memory and measured wall/train/inference latency; empty,one,100 and holey histories; perturb masked IDs including out-of-vocabulary values, masked task masks and current target action in eval/cloned train modes. Valid historical actions may affect predictions. Verify inherited g0/R12 states and CPU RNG, zero-start predictions, distinct private Parameter/storage and Dice buffers, identical initial clones and no implicit host reset after cloning. Shared64 override must reproduce archived R14-open predictions, Dice updates and gradients. Open final scorer layers in a diagnostic clone before checking live hidden gradients: all are zero upstream initially by design. Use detached leaf flat inputs to isolate per-head trunk gradients; do not confuse shared embedding gradients with trunk ownership. Check clone-specific Dice updates and optimizer registration of every clone. Full numerical checks must be charged to the host. Selection uses all four validation tasks under the supplied tie breakers; report task AUC/Logloss, reference deltas and host-supported predeclared slices with counts, marking insufficient positives/negatives; only request paired user-cluster bootstrap if authorized predictions/user grouping are available, which they are not here.